},
{
"text": "A",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
142.70486005147293,
87.13541030883789,
167.8958333333332
],
"fontSize": 25.190973281860266
},
{
"text": "cute coronary syndrome remains one of the leading",
"rect": [
83.47222010294597,
157.7395515441894,
290.1215235392253,
167.73955790201813
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828738
},
{
"text": "causes of morbidity and mortality globally despite ad-",
"rect": [
83.47222010294597,
145.76038487752265,
290.05208015441895,
155.7603912353515
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828852
},
{
"text": "vances in primary and secondary preventive treatments",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
133.71179072062165,
290.0868097941081,
143.71179707845047
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828823
},
{
"text": "(1). Histologic and intravascular imaging investigations",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
121.74998092651362,
290.06943702697754,
131.74998728434232
],
"fontSize": 10.00000635782871
},
{
"text": "have demonstrated that most cases of acute coronary",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
109.78817113240545,
290.06943702697754,
119.78817749023429
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828838
},
{
"text": "syndrome are due to the rupture of large and lipid-rich",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
97.80900446573882,
290.1215235392253,
107.80901082356755
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828724
},
{
"text": "atheromas (2). Thus, the early, accurate identification",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
85.7604103088378,
290.1215235392253,
95.76041666666653
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828724
},
{
"text": "of these high-risk vulnerable plaques is of importance.",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
73.79861640930162,
290.1215235392253,
83.7986068725585
],
"fontSize": 9.999990463256879
},
{
"text": "Gray-scale intravascular US can provide a unique op-",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
61.81944974263498,
290.15625317891437,
71.81944020589187
],
"fontSize": 9.999990463256886
},
{
"text": "portunity to visualize vulnerable plaque features, in-",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
49.857624053955,
290.1041666666667,
59.85763041178372
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828717
},
{
"text": "cluding attenuated plaque and echolucent plaque (3).",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
37.809045791625934,
290.1041666666667,
47.80903625488269
],
"fontSize": 9.999990463256758
},
{
"text": "These features have been reported to be associated with",
"rect": [
71.96180025736491,
25.847220102945823,
290.1215235392253,
35.847226460774664
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828841
},
{
"text": "worse clinical outcomes (4,5). However, intravascular",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
157.7395515441894,
527.0486036936442,
167.73955790201813
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828738
},
{
"text": "US is an invasive, expensive technique and is not widely",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
145.76038487752265,
526.9097169240315,
155.7603912353515
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828852
},
{
"text": "available in most laboratories.",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
133.71179072062165,
425.7986068725586,
143.71179707845047
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828823
},
{
"text": "Coronary CT angiography (CCTA) is now a first-line",
"rect": [
320.85069020589196,
121.74998092651362,
527.0659764607748,
131.74998728434232
],
"fontSize": 10.00000635782871
},
{
"text": "noninvasive imaging modality for diagnosing coronary ar-",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
109.78817113240545,
526.9791603088379,
119.78817749023429
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828838
},
{
"text": "tery disease (CAD). Recently, qualitative plaque features",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
97.80900446573882,
526.9791603088379,
107.80901082356755
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828724
},
{
"text": "and quantitative attenuation-based plaque metrics at CCTA",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
85.7604103088378,
526.9270896911621,
95.76041666666653
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828724
},
{
"text": "have demonstrated prognostic value for acute coronary syn-",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
73.79861640930162,
527.013889948527,
83.7986068725585
],
"fontSize": 9.999990463256879
},
{
"text": "drome (6–8). However, these conventional anatomic CCTA",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
61.81944974263498,
526.9965330759684,
71.81944020589187
],
"fontSize": 9.999990463256886
},
{
"text": "parameters neglect the heterogeneity and spatial complexity",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
49.857624053955,
526.9444465637207,
59.85763041178372
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828717
},
{
"text": "in plaques. Previous studies have shown that the anatomic",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
37.809045791625934,
526.9791603088379,
47.80903625488269
],
"fontSize": 9.999990463256758
},
{
"text": "plaque features at CCTA had only a modest correlation with",
"rect": [
308.8541666666667,
25.847220102945823,
526.9791603088379,
35.847226460774664
],
"fontSize": 10.000006357828841
},
{
"text": "Background:",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
434.475699742635,
115.45138359069824,
442.47917302449537
],
"fontSize": 8.003473281860352
},
{
"text": "A noninvasive coronary CT angiography (CCTA)–based radiomics technique may facilitate the identification of",
"rect": [
123.95833333333333,
434.0416825612385,
492.1354293823242,
442.5486323038736
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635129
},
{
"text": "vulnerable plaques and patients at risk for future adverse events.",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
424.5798505147297,
293.17708015441895,
433.08678436279286
],
"fontSize": 8.50693384806317
},
{
"text": "Purpose:",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
402.86111005147285,
106.2326431274414,
410.86458333333326
],
"fontSize": 8.003473281860408
},
{
"text": "To assess whether a CCTA-based radiomic signature (RS) of vulnerable plaques defined with intravascular US was",
"rect": [
114.34027353922525,
402.5138931274413,
488.68055343627924,
411.02082697550446
],
"fontSize": 8.50693384806317
},
{
"text": "associated with increased risk for future major adverse cardiac events (MACE).",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
392.98263359069813,
341.5451367696126,
401.48958333333326
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635129
},
{
"text": "Materials and Methods:",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
371.3506933848062,
144.70486640930176,
379.3541666666666
],
"fontSize": 8.003473281860352
},
{
"text": "In a retrospective study, an RS of vulnerable plaques was developed and validated using intravascular US as",
"rect": [
153.17708651224774,
370.9166444142659,
503.8541634877523,
379.42359415690095
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635072
},
{
"text": "the reference standard. The RS development data set included patients first undergoing CCTA and then intravascular US within",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
361.4548600514729,
505.1909923553467,
369.961809794108
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635072
},
{
"text": "3 months between June 2013 and December 2020 at one tertiary hospital. The development set was randomly assigned to training",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
351.9062277475992,
513.2812658945719,
360.4131774902343
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635129
},
{
"text": "and validation sets at a 7:3 ratio. Diagnostic performance was assessed internally and externally from three tertiary hospitals using",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
342.44444338480616,
508.45484733581543,
350.9513931274413
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635129
},
{
"text": "the area under the curve (AUC). The prognostic value of the RS for predicting MACE was evaluated in a prospective cohort with",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
332.9826431274413,
508.2117875417074,
341.4895769755044
],
"fontSize": 8.506933848063113
},
{
"text": "suspected coronary artery disease between April 2018 and March 2019. Multivariable Cox regression analysis was used to evaluate",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
323.43402671813953,
510.59028307596844,
331.9409764607746
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635072
},
{
"text": "the RS and conventional anatomic plaque features (eg, segment involvement score) for predicting MACE.",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
313.97222646077466,
431.82291984558105,
322.4791603088378
],
"fontSize": 8.506933848063113
},
{
"text": "Results:",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
292.32291348775215,
103.95833651224771,
300.32638676961255
],
"fontSize": 8.003473281860408
},
{
"text": "The RS development data set included 419 lesions from 225 patients (mean age, 64 years ± 10 [SD]; 68 men), while the",
"rect": [
112.44791348775227,
291.9062690734862,
507.6909859975179,
300.4132029215494
],
"fontSize": 8.50693384806317
},
{
"text": "prognostic cohort included 1020 lesions from 708 patients (mean age, 62 years ± 11; 498 men). Sixteen radiomic features, includ-",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
282.4444370269774,
511.9791825612386,
290.95138676961255
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635129
},
{
"text": "ing two shape features and 14 textural features, were selected to build the RS. The RS yielded a moderate to good AUC in the",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
272.89585240681953,
496.63195610046387,
281.40278625488276
],
"fontSize": 8.506933848063227
},
{
"text": "training, validation, internal, and external test sets (AUC = 0.81, 0.75, 0.80, and 0.77, respectively). A high RS (≥1.07) was inde-",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
263.4340203603108,
508.9062531789144,
271.94097010294587
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635072
},
{
"text": "pendently associated with MACE over a median 3-year follow-up (hazard ratio, 2.01;",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
253.8854357401529,
364.13194338480633,
262.392369588216
],
"fontSize": 8.506933848063113
},
{
"text": "P",
"rect": [
365.3298695882161,
253.8854357401529,
370.06945610046387,
262.392369588216
],
"fontSize": 8.506933848063113
},
{
"text": "= .005).",
"rect": [
372.1527735392253,
253.8854357401529,
398.3333269755046,
262.392369588216
],
"fontSize": 8.506933848063113
},
{
"text": "Conclusion:",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
232.25349553426096,
112.5173568725586,
240.25695292154938
],
"fontSize": 8.003457387288421
},
{
"text": "A coronary CT angiography–derived radiomic signature of coronary plaque enabled the detection of vulnerable plaques",
"rect": [
120.98957697550456,
231.81943066914863,
513.819440205892,
240.3263804117838
],
"fontSize": 8.506949742635157
},
{
"text": "that were associated with increased risk for future adverse cardiac outcomes.",
"rect": [
83.94096692403157,
222.35766220092762,
332.2916666666667,
230.8645960489908
],
"fontSize": 8.50693384806317
},
{
